                <div class="service-detail-points governance-content-section">
                    <h3 class="governance-subtitle">Why Choose Sonagra &amp; Company?</h3>
                    <p>Corporate governance requires a combination of regulatory understanding, professional judgement and attention to detail. A governance framework should work in practice while meeting the obligations applicable to the organisation.</p>
                    <div class="governance-feature-list">
                        <article><h4>Regulatory Clarity</h4><p>Helping management understand applicable corporate and governance obligations.</p></article>
                        <article><h4>Practical Governance</h4><p>Developing processes and policies that can be effectively implemented within the organisation.</p></article>
                        <article><h4>Board-Level Perspective</h4><p>Considering the responsibilities of directors, committees and management when addressing governance matters.</p></article>
                        <article><h4>Compliance Discipline</h4><p>Helping businesses identify gaps and maintain more consistent statutory and regulatory processes.</p></article>
                        <article><h4>Ongoing Advisory Support</h4><p>Providing professional guidance as governance requirements and business circumstances evolve.</p></article>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="service-detail-points governance-content-section">
                    <h3>Strengthening Board &amp; Committee Effectiveness</h3>
                    <p>The Board of Directors plays a central role in corporate governance. An appropriately structured board, clearly defined responsibilities and effective committee functioning can improve oversight and support better corporate decision-making.</p>
                    <div class="service-detail-list">
                        <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Board composition and appointment of directors</h3><p>Guidance on executive, non-executive and independent director requirements based on applicable obligations.</p></div></article>
                        <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Roles and responsibilities of directors</h3><p>Clear advisory on responsibilities of directors and governance accountability expectations.</p></div></article>
                        <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Constitution and functioning of committees</h3><p>Support for Audit, NRC, CSR, Risk Management, Stakeholders Relationship and industry-specific committee matters.</p></div></article>
                        <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Board meeting processes and documentation</h3><p>Improvement of board process discipline, records and governance documentation standards.</p></div></article>
                        <article><span>05</span><div><h3>Governance disclosures and reporting</h3><p>Structured support for governance disclosures, board-related reporting and compliance alignment.</p></div></article>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="service-detail-points governance-content-section">
                    <h3>Governance Policies &amp; Frameworks</h3>
                    <p>Well-drafted policies provide consistency in how important corporate matters are handled. We assist with developing, reviewing and updating governance policies including:</p>
                    <ul class="governance-bullet-list">
                        <li>Code of Conduct</li>
                        <li>Insider Trading Policy</li>
                        <li>Related Party Transactions Policy</li>
                        <li>Whistleblower Policy</li>
                        <li>Board Evaluation Framework</li>
                        <li>Other governance and compliance policies applicable to the organisation</li>
                    </ul>
                    <img class="governance-inline-image" src="/images/pexels-n-voitkevich-8062299-r9d7uuyb9fhu91oqw1a7we7b37lyhv8mb4ifglwsq0.jpg.png" alt="Governance policy documentation" loading="lazy" />
                </div>

                <div class="service-detail-points governance-content-section">
                    <h3>Secretarial Compliance Advisory Services</h3>
                    <p>Corporate governance and secretarial compliance are closely connected. We help organisations review and improve their secretarial compliance framework through:</p>
                    <ul class="governance-bullet-list">
                        <li>Review of applicable corporate compliance requirements</li>
                        <li>Board and general meeting compliance</li>
                        <li>Statutory records and documentation</li>
                        <li>Regulatory filings and disclosures</li>
                        <li>Governance-related ROC and SEBI compliance</li>
                        <li>Compliance review and corrective recommendations</li>
                        <li>Assistance with ongoing compliance monitoring</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="service-detail-points governance-content-section">
                    <img class="governance-inline-image governance-review-image" src="/images/23514.jpg.png" alt="Corporate governance compliance review and audit" loading="lazy" />
                    <h3>Corporate Governance Compliance Review &amp; Audit</h3>
                    <p>Regular governance reviews can help identify gaps before they become significant compliance or reputational concerns. We assist with periodic reviews and internal assessments, followed by practical recommendations aligned with Companies Act and applicable SEBI governance requirements.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="service-detail-points governance-content-section">
                    <h3>Corporate Governance Reporting &amp; Disclosures</h3>
                    <p>Transparent reporting is an important part of effective governance. We assist with preparation and review of reports and disclosures covering board functioning, committee activities, governance practices and regulatory obligations.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="governance-image-grid governance-report-image-grid">
                    <img src="/images/18057-rsbrihzv7obcw7ijyj7egitryllpwl30ou7pimn8lc.jpg.png" alt="Corporate governance reporting reference image" loading="lazy" />
                    <img src="/images/pexels-n-voitkevich-8062299-r9d7uuyb9fhu91oqw1a7we7b37lyhv8mb4ifglwsq0_1.jpg.png" alt="Governance support reference image" loading="lazy" />
                </div>

                <div class="service-detail-points governance-content-section governance-support-split">
                    <h3>Governance Support for Listed &amp; Growing Companies</h3>
                    <p>Governance requirements vary significantly depending on the nature, size and regulatory status of a business. Listed companies may have extensive disclosure and board-related obligations, while growing private companies may need stronger governance processes as ownership and operations become more complex.</p>
                    <p>Our professional assistance can be relevant for:</p>
                    <ul class="governance-check-list">
                        <li>Listed companies</li>
                        <li>Unlisted public companies</li>
                        <li>Private limited companies</li>
                        <li>Growing and professionally managed businesses</li>
                        <li>Companies preparing for capital market activities</li>
                        <li>Businesses undergoing ownership or structural changes</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <section class="formation-faq-section service-detail-points">
                    <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
                    <details>
                        <summary>What are Corporate Governance Advisory Services?</summary>
                        <p>These services help companies establish and maintain governance frameworks for board functioning, committee responsibilities, policies, compliance, disclosures and accountability.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>What are Secretarial Compliance Advisory Services?</summary>
                        <p>These services focus on corporate secretarial requirements including board and shareholder processes, statutory records, filings, disclosures and compliance reviews.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Why is corporate governance important for a company?</summary>
                        <p>Effective governance promotes accountability and transparency, improves oversight and helps businesses manage regulatory obligations confidently.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Can you advise on board composition and committees?</summary>
                        <p>Yes. We provide advisory on board composition and key committees including Audit, NRC, CSR, RMC and SRC-related matters.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Do you provide corporate governance compliance reviews?</summary>
                        <p>Yes. We conduct periodic reviews to identify compliance gaps and recommend practical corrective measures based on applicable regulations.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Do you support listed companies on governance requirements?</summary>
                        <p>Yes. We assist listed and regulated entities with governance, disclosure and compliance responsibilities under applicable frameworks.</p>
                    </details>
